FEX on Android: RootFS lookups without the openat2 syscall.

Guest open/openat of an absolute path tries the RootFS first with openat2(RESOLVE_IN_ROOT), which
Android blocks. OpenInRoot (LinuxSyscalls/InRootResolver.cpp) does the same lookup in userspace,
following openat2(2): one component at a time with openat(O_PATH | O_NOFOLLOW) from RootFSFD;
absolute paths and links restart at RootFSFD; ".." at the root stays there; procfs magic links fail
with EXDEV; more than 40 links fail with ELOOP. The last component is opened with the guest's flags
plus O_NOFOLLOW, so a link created meanwhile is walked again. FileManager::Open and Openat use it;
the EXDEV and host fallbacks stay. unittests/APITests/InRootResolver.cpp tests it.

